<title>GERMANY: German Oct/April sugar sales slightly up yr/yr.</title>
<headline>German Oct/April sugar sales slightly up yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>German sugar sales in the first seven months of the 1996/97 (October/September) season totalled 1.58 million tonnes, slightly up from 1.57 million in October/April 95/96, sugar industry association WVZ data showed on Monday.</p>
<p>Sugar sales in April of 245,201 tonnes compared with 225,919 in April 1996.</p>
<p>Sugar production in April was 1,591 tonnes (1,744).</p>
<p>Stocks at the end of April were 1.92 million tonnes versus 1.70 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>Carry-in stocks on October 1, 1996 had been 239,562 tonnes (250,854 a year earlier).</p>
<p>April imports of 7,599 tonnes were up from 6,419 tonnes a year earlier while exports of 141,003 tonnes compared with 68,129 in April 1996.</p>
<p>Cumulative details (in tonnes) --</p>
<p>				  Oct/April 96/97  Oct/April 95/96</p>
<p>    Domestic sugar output 4,184,057	  3,810,684</p>
<p>    Imports			46,982	     66,069</p>
<p>    Exports		     969,642	    851,221</p>
<p>    Domestic sales	  1,578,066	  1,571,982</p>
<p>--Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
